{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "html": "<p>The domains are the tell. Fifteen years on the same address, renewed every October by someone who never expected an audience and got one anyway. I have been keeping a list since 2019, and it has never once grown.</p>",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "html": "<p>What they share is not taste. Some are beautiful and most are not. It is a refusal to move — off the address, off the software, off the habit — which turns out to be the rarest thing on the web.</p>",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "html": "<div class=\"kg-card kg-callout-card kg-callout-card-accent\"><div class=\"kg-callout-emoji\">💡</div><div class=\"kg-callout-text\">If you are looking for the list itself, it is at the end of this issue — and every link on it was checked the week this went out.</div></div>",
      "id": "callout-accent"
    },
    {
      "html": "<h2 id=\"who-is-actually-paying\">Who is actually paying</h2>",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "html": "<p>Three of the four hundred are paid for by estates. Two are paid for by universities that forgot they were paying. The rest are individuals, and their renewal dates cluster in October for a reason nobody has explained to my satisfaction.</p>",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "html": "<blockquote>A site that outlives three platform migrations is not nostalgic. It is just paid for.<br>Perennial Notes, 2019</blockquote>",
      "id": "quote"
    },
    {
      "html": "<p>I asked eleven of them why October. The answers divided cleanly:</p>",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "html": "<ul><li>Four said the date meant nothing at all, and were mildly annoyed to be asked.</li><li>Three said it was simply when they had money, which is the honest version of the same answer.</li><li>Two said October was when their first host used to bill them. That host closed in 2013.</li></ul>",
      "id": "list-bullet"
    },
    {
      "html": "<figure class=\"kg-card kg-bookmark-card\"><a class=\"kg-bookmark-container\" href=\"https://perennial.orbit-weekly.example/the-web-is-not-a-feed/\"><div class=\"kg-bookmark-content\"><div class=\"kg-bookmark-title\">The Web Is Not A Feed, And Never Was</div><div class=\"kg-bookmark-description\">An argument for the personal site, made by someone who has kept one since 2004 and has the logs to prove it.</div><div class=\"kg-bookmark-metadata\"><img class=\"kg-bookmark-icon\" src=\"https://orbit-weekly.example/images/icon.svg\" alt=\"\"><span class=\"kg-bookmark-author\">perennial.orbit-weekly.example</span><span class=\"kg-bookmark-publisher\">Perennial Notes</span></div></div><div class=\"kg-bookmark-thumbnail\"><img src=\"https://orbit-weekly.example/images/feature-05.svg\" alt=\"\" onerror=\"this.style.display = 'none'\"></div></a></figure>",
      "id": "bookmark-thumbnail"
    },
    {
      "html": "<h3 id=\"the-renewal-arithmetic\">The renewal arithmetic</h3>",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "html": "<p>A domain costs about twelve dollars a year. Hosting a static site costs nothing at three of the four common hosts. The whole obligation, then, is one dollar a month and one afternoon a decade.</p>\n",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "html": "<!--kg-card-begin: html-->\n<table><thead><tr><th>Cohort</th><th>Still live</th><th>Moved</th><th>Gone</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Registered before 2000</td><td>61</td><td>14</td><td>109</td></tr><tr><td>2000 – 2009</td><td>183</td><td>52</td><td>240</td></tr><tr><td>2010 – 2014</td><td>156</td><td>88</td><td>301</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!--kg-card-end: html-->\n",
      "id": "table"
    },
    {
      "html": "<p>The counting itself is unglamorous. I run one request a month against each address and record what comes back, which is <a href=\"https://orbit-weekly.example/the-list/\">fourteen lines of shell</a> and a text file:</p>",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "html": "<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">#!/usr/bin/env bash\nwhile read -r host; do\n  code=$(curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' \\\n    --max-time 10 \"https://$host/\" || echo 000)\n  printf '%s\\t%s\\t%s\\n' \"$(date -I)\" \"$host\" \"$code\"\ndone &lt; hosts.txt &gt;&gt; log.tsv</code></pre>",
      "id": "code"
    },
    {
      "html": "<p>Anything that answers <code>200</code> twice in a row goes on the list. Anything that answers <code>000</code> for three months comes off it, and I check by hand before it does.</p>",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "html": "<div class=\"kg-card kg-toggle-card\" data-kg-toggle-state=\"close\">\n            <div class=\"kg-toggle-heading\">\n                <h4 class=\"kg-toggle-heading-text\">Why not just use the Internet Archive?</h4>\n                <button class=\"kg-toggle-card-icon\" aria-label=\"Expand toggle to read content\">\n                    <svg id=\"Regular\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\">\n                        <path class=\"cls-1\" d=\"M23.25,7.311,12.53,18.03a.749.749,0,0,1-1.06,0L.75,7.311\"></path>\n                    </svg>\n                </button>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"kg-toggle-content\"><p>Because the Archive tells you a page existed, not that someone is still paying for it. Those are different questions, and only the second one predicts next October.</p></div>\n        </div>",
      "id": "toggle"
    },
    {
      "html": "<h2 id=\"what-the-pages-look-like\">What the pages look like</h2>",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "html": "<p>Seven of them, photographed on the same afternoon at the same window width, in the order they were registered:</p>",
      "id": null
    },
    {
      "html": "<figure class=\"kg-card kg-gallery-card kg-width-wide kg-card-hascaption\"><div class=\"kg-gallery-container\"><div class=\"kg-gallery-row\"><div class=\"kg-gallery-image\"><img src=\"https://orbit-weekly.example/images/feature-01.svg\" width=\"1600\" height=\"900\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Homepage 1\"></div><div class=\"kg-gallery-image\"><img src=\"https://orbit-weekly.example/images/feature-02.svg\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1100\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Homepage 2\"></div><div class=\"kg-gallery-image\"><img src=\"https://orbit-weekly.example/images/feature-03.svg\" width=\"1600\" height=\"900\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Homepage 3\"></div></div><div class=\"kg-gallery-row\"><div class=\"kg-gallery-image\"><img src=\"https://orbit-weekly.example/images/feature-04.svg\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1100\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Homepage 4\"></div><div class=\"kg-gallery-image\"><img src=\"https://orbit-weekly.example/images/feature-05.svg\" width=\"1600\" height=\"900\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"Homepage 5\"></div></div></div><figcaption>Seven homepages, August 2026. Two have not changed since 2011.</figcaption></figure>",
      "id": "gallery-5-caption"
    },
    {
      "html": "<p>There is an audio version of the interviews, if you would rather hear the October answers in the original voices:</p>",
      "id": null
    },
